From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Thu, 4 Sep 2026 14:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] detector: make the NNAPI delegate optional

Two problems on a glibc/Halium target, both fatal:

 1. init_common() throws outright when the Neural Networks HAL is not
    registered in hwservicemanager. That makes libfart unusable on every
    device whose vendor ships no NNAPI HAL, and on all non-Halium machines
    where hwservicemanager does not exist at all - even though every NNAPI
    call site already falls back to CPU cleanly. A missing accelerator
    should not be a hard failure.

 2. The delegate is reached through the C API in
    tensorflow/lite/delegates/nnapi/nnapi_delegate_c_api.h. Upstream
    TensorFlow Lite builds that C wrapper as a separate CMake target, so a
    stock libtensorflow-lite.so exports the C++ StatefulNnApiDelegate but
    not TfLiteNnapiDelegateCreate/Delete/OptionsDefault. libfart then links
    with undefined references, which a consumer built with
    -Wl,--no-undefined cannot link against.

Guard the whole NNAPI path behind FART_ENABLE_NNAPI, off by default. The
interpreters run on CPU (XNNPACK on aarch64), which is what actually happens
on these devices anyway: TFLite's NNAPI delegate dlopens Android's
libneuralnetworks.so, which is bionic-side and not reachable from a glibc
process.

Distributions that build against a TensorFlow Lite providing the C wrapper,
on a device with an NNAPI HAL, can restore the old behaviour with
-DFART_ENABLE_NNAPI=1.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
--- a/src/detector.cpp
+++ b/src/detector.cpp
@@ -20,7 +20,9 @@
 #include <opencv2/imgproc.hpp>
 
 #include "tensorflow/lite/kernels/register.h"
+#if FART_ENABLE_NNAPI
 #include "tensorflow/lite/delegates/nnapi/nnapi_delegate_c_api.h"
+#endif
 
 using json = nlohmann::json;
 namespace fs = std::filesystem;
@@ -72,8 +74,10 @@
                           const std::string& recognition_model_path,
                           const std::string& anti_spoof_model_path)
 {
+#if FART_ENABLE_NNAPI
     if (!find_hal("android.hardware.neuralnetworks"))
         throw std::runtime_error("Neural Networks HAL not found in hwservicemanager");
+#endif
 
     detection_model_ = tflite::FlatBufferModel::BuildFromFile(detection_model_path.c_str());
     if (!detection_model_)
@@ -84,6 +88,7 @@
     if (!detector_)
         throw std::runtime_error("Failed to build detection interpreter");
 
+#if FART_ENABLE_NNAPI
     TfLiteNnapiDelegateOptions nnapi_options = TfLiteNnapiDelegateOptionsDefault();
     nnapi_options.allow_fp16 = true;
     nnapi_options.disallow_nnapi_cpu = false;
@@ -99,6 +104,7 @@
             nnapi_detection_delegate_ = nullptr;
         }
     }
+#endif
 
     if (detector_->AllocateTensors() != kTfLiteOk)
         throw std::runtime_error("Failed to allocate tensors for detection model");
@@ -111,6 +117,7 @@
     if (!recognizer_)
         throw std::runtime_error("Failed to build recognition interpreter");
 
+#if FART_ENABLE_NNAPI
     nnapi_recognition_delegate_ = TfLiteNnapiDelegateCreate(&nnapi_options);
     if (!nnapi_recognition_delegate_) {
         g_debug("Failed to create NNAPI delegate for recognition model, falling back to CPU");
@@ -122,6 +129,7 @@
             nnapi_recognition_delegate_ = nullptr;
         }
     }
+#endif
 
     if (recognizer_->AllocateTensors() != kTfLiteOk)
         throw std::runtime_error("Failed to allocate tensors for recognition model");
@@ -137,6 +145,7 @@
         if (!anti_spoofer_)
             throw std::runtime_error("Failed to build anti-spoof interpreter");
 
+#if FART_ENABLE_NNAPI
         nnapi_spoof_delegate_ = TfLiteNnapiDelegateCreate(&nnapi_options);
         if (!nnapi_spoof_delegate_) {
             g_debug("Failed to create NNAPI delegate for anti-spoof model, falling back to CPU");
@@ -148,6 +157,7 @@
                 nnapi_spoof_delegate_ = nullptr;
             }
         }
+#endif
 
         if (anti_spoofer_->AllocateTensors() != kTfLiteOk)
             throw std::runtime_error("Failed to allocate tensors for anti-spoof model");
@@ -181,6 +191,7 @@
 
 FaceDetector::~FaceDetector()
 {
+#if FART_ENABLE_NNAPI
     if (nnapi_detection_delegate_) {
         TfLiteNnapiDelegateDelete(nnapi_detection_delegate_);
         nnapi_detection_delegate_ = nullptr;
@@ -193,6 +204,7 @@
         TfLiteNnapiDelegateDelete(nnapi_spoof_delegate_);
         nnapi_spoof_delegate_ = nullptr;
     }
+#endif
 }
 
 std::vector<FaceDetector::DetectedFace>
